 :recommended-boundary
 {:name :private-owner-readback-decoder
  :input :bounded-captured-wire-string-only
  :not-input [:parsed-value :caller-review-context :path-to-reread :arbitrary-metadata-bearing-value]
  :semantics
  ["Keep frozen safe_reference law, nine frozen files, digest and owner unchanged. All direct application event/partition input still passes frozen require-plain-data!/validate-event! before Clio or serialization. A raw tainted object must never be routed through pr-str then this decoder."
   "Capture bytes once within the existing lock/read authority; enforce byte, line/event-count and nesting/work limits; strict UTF-8 decoding (reject invalid encodings) to immutable string. For permit/review, hash those same captured bytes, compare exact pinned digests, and decode that same immutable string, never hash a file then reopen it. Mutable Buffer supplied by caller is not a custody guarantee; capture/copy into private immutable representation before checking."
   "Apply a small conservative lexical refusal gate to that exact string BEFORE owner read-one: reject ^ and # outside double-quoted strings at any depth, reject semicolon/comments and backslash/character syntax outside strings, distinguish escaped quotes/backslashes inside strings, and refuse unfinished strings/escapes. No quote-count regex: correct string/escape state is necessary. Rejecting all dispatch outside strings excludes records, unknown and built-in tags, #_, reader conditionals/eval, sets, namespaced-map dispatch. Literal ^/#/semicolon inside strings are data, not metadata syntax. Owner remains sole actual EDN decoder and exact-one-form checker; this gate is NOT a second EDN parser, ledger engine or canonicalization kernel."
   "Call fixed pinned clio.shape.edn/read-one exactly on the gated captured string. Do not expose a public function accepting an already-read object. Recursively inspect the resulting tree BEFORE fresh construction: allow only exact plain array/hash maps, exact vectors and frozen scalar domain; refuse records, symbols, lists, sets, tagged/host values and custom wrappers; visit keys too. Metadata on collection nodes may only be the exact four keyword keys :row :col :end-row :end-col with positive safe integer values and nondecreasing lexicographic start/end, consistent with byte/text bounds. Refuse unknown keys, empty metadata, unexpected metadata on scalars. Validate before removal; do not use select-keys to discard unknown metadata. Location shape alone is NOT provenance; gate plus direct private call establishes its source."
   "Construct fresh metadata-free plain maps/vectors recursively. Run unchanged frozen law over complete decoded partition/event BEFORE owner canonicalization and desktop replay; errors are constant input/cause-free Oikos diagnostics. Safe identity and schema checks remain unchanged; no metadata enters event identity."
   "For histories, decode captured nonblank ledger lines privately, preserving ordering/duplicates, then call existing owner domain canonicalize on decoded partitions plus new already-safe event. Reuse owner schema validation/history/admission/locking/append; do not call canonicalize-files on paths after gating because it rereads and reintroduces metadata. Owner append may internally reread under its own lock as designed; do not replace its admission engine. External writers not honoring adapter coordination lock remain an explicit concurrency threat; prove locking assumptions before append."
   "For authenticated parent evidence, prefer freshly construct only exact closed expected/artifact/trusted-review fields from the authenticated same-byte read, validate types/keys, then frozen qualified?. This transfers authenticated evidence, never manufactures approval from an untrusted passed-in map. No hypothetical global immutable provenance service is required."]
  :why-not-owner-change "An additive owner options/decode primitive could suppress locations but still needs raw metadata refusal; owner changes require new source SHA/digest qualification and downstream pin review. Not necessary to prove this adapter design; do not add a replacement kernel."
  :why-not-metadata-whitelist-alone "Actual ^{:row 99} is accepted and overwritten by owner locations; four-key inspection cannot distinguish forged syntax. Never sanitize caller objects even with identical location maps."
  :framer-reuse "S1A frame remains a useful qualified restricted protocol component, not a complete byte grammar gate for this boolean-bearing domain. A new tiny lexical refusal gate is new adapter source requiring independent review; it does not amend S1A or activate its held BB operational adapter."}
